    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. specifically regarding the testing and staging gates, i'm worried about things slipping through that automated tests might miss. what are some common things that tend to bypass those gates and cause issues once we hit production?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Common issues that bypass automated tests in fintech often include race conditions, timing-dependent side effects, and microservice failures that don't reproduce in isolated unit tests. Static analysis tools also frequently miss complex business logic errors, such as undefined edge cases in currency calculations or permission hierarchy misunderstandings. Additionally, configuration drift in staging environments or insufficient integration of external payment gateways and third-party APIs during testing can lead to production failures that automated scripts fail to detect. To mitigate this, prioritize contract testing between services, add manual approval gates for critical financial operations, and ensure your staging environment closely mirrors production's hyperscaling and latency characteristics.",
      "source": "target",
