      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i get that. it's usually those \"silent\" bugs that kill us. i guess i'm just worried about the \"gatekeeper\" aspect of it—how do we ensure that the gates actually stay effective over time and don't just become easy to circumvent or ignore as the team scales? is there a way to monitor if the gates are actually being bypassed or if they're just being treated as a checkbox?",
